SQLite
------
The SQLite extension (sqlite/, released as the sift-sqlite archive) is compiled against the loadable-extension headers
(sqlite3.h, sqlite3ext.h) of the SQLite development package of the build machine and loads into the SQLite library of the
application that uses it. It contains no SQLite source code and links no SQLite library. SQLite is in the public domain
(https://sqlite.org/copyright.html). The host implementation in sqlite/host/ is not PostgreSQL's: it is a small re-implementation, written
for this repository under the PostgreSQL License, of the slice of the PostgreSQL backend API that the engine sources in src/ use.
The sift-sqlite archive includes this file because it carries the same Unicode tables and Snowball stemmer as pg_sift.

Not distributed with pg_sift
-------------------------
The checks under tools/ and bench/ download reference data at run time (the
Unicode Character Database, the snowball-data English vocabulary, Simple
English Wikipedia, GeoNames) and compare against other engines; none of it is
part of this repository or of the installed extension.
